# What this machine IS. Sourced by install.sh before anything else, so these
# answer questions install.sh would otherwise have to guess from whatever
# environment it happens to be running in.
#
# The guessing is the bug this replaces: the graphical branch keyed on
# WAYLAND_DISPLAY, which exists when you run install.sh by hand and does not
# when dotfiles-sync re-runs it from cron — so a graphical machine configured
# itself differently depending on who invoked it.
#
# Copy to hosts/<hostname>/host.env and commit. A machine with no hosts/<name>/
# directory is unaffected by all of this: link() no-ops on a missing source.

# Graphical workstation: render the theme and link hypr/.
GRAPHICAL=0

# Sudoless docker: membership in the docker group. That group is effectively
# passwordless root -- anything that can reach the socket can bind-mount / and
# chroot into it, which means every process in your session, coding agents and
# a malicious pip install included, not just you at a terminal. What it
# defeats is the sudo password gate, and with it faillock; LUKS still protects
# the disk at rest, that threat is unrelated.
#
# 0 (default): provisioning does not touch the group. `docker` needs sudo, or
# rootless Docker once the VM suite shows compose works under cgroup v2
# delegation. 1: provisioning adds you and `ergon doctor` warns on every run,
# so the trade-off stays visible instead of fading into "that's just how this
# machine is". Full writeup: ergon explain security.
#
# Provisioning only ever ADDS for this knob, never removes: flipping it back
# to 0 does not undo a membership granted while it was 1, because a
# reprovision that silently drops your own session's docker access is a worse
# surprise than the one this knob exists to fix. `ergon doctor` reports that
# drift instead.
DOCKER_GROUP=0

# Tailscale: run tailscaled, so this machine can join a tailnet (ERGON-39).
# The package is in the base and the firewall already admits tailscale0, but
# the daemon is a choice, not a default: it used to start on every machine.
# Provisioning asks when it first creates this file; ERGON_TAILSCALE=1 answers
# for an unattended run. Like DOCKER_GROUP, provisioning only ever ENABLES for
# this: setting it back to 0 does not stop a tailscaled you are logged in to.
TAILSCALE=0

# Where screenshots are written. Empty means ~/Pictures/Screenshots. A host
# that mirrors captures somewhere names the folder its watcher reads, e.g.
# SCREENSHOT_DIR="$HOME/screenshots-outgoing". install.sh hands it to the
# session (environment.d), so a change takes effect at the next login.
SCREENSHOT_DIR=""

# Free-form, for anything that wants to branch on machine class rather than
# hostname. Used by nothing yet — do not add consumers without a reason.
PROFILE=server

# Optional package bundles, space separated: `ergon-bundle list` shows what
# exists and what each costs (science stacks, editors, and apps such as
# discord and moonlight).
#
# Recorded here rather than merely applied, so reprovisioning reproduces the
# machine. `ergon-bundle add/remove` edits this line for you; provisioning runs
# `ergon-bundle sync` against it.
#
# Bundles added from a source (ergon-bundle add github:me/overlay//fleet) are
# NOT listed here: they are copied into hosts/<host>/bundles/<name>/, and that
# directory is the record. Commit it with this file (git add -f).
BUNDLES=""
